(EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This Employment Contract is entered into on June 1, 2024, between Harlow & Associates LLP) Tj T*
(\("Employer"\) and the individual identified below \("Employee"\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(POSITION AND DUTIES) Tj T*
(The Employee is hired as a Senior Legal Analyst. The Employee shall perform duties including) Tj T*
(contract review, legal research, regulatory compliance analysis, and client advisory support.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(COMPENSATION) Tj T*
(The Employee shall receive an annual base salary of ninety-two thousand dollars \($92,000\),) Tj T*
(payable bi-weekly. The Employee is eligible for an annual performance bonus of up to 15%) Tj T*
(of base salary, subject to performance review.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(BENEFITS) Tj T*
(The Employee is entitled to: 20 days paid annual leave, 10 days sick leave, health insurance) Tj T*
(coverage under the Employer's group plan, and participation in the 401\(k\) plan with 4%) Tj T*
(employer matching.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(PROBATIONARY PERIOD) Tj T*
(The first ninety \(90\) days of employment constitute a probationary period during which either) Tj T*
(party may terminate the contract with one \(1\) week written notice.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(NON-COMPETE CLAUSE) Tj T*
(For a period of twelve \(12\) months following termination, the Employee agrees not to engage) Tj T*
(in any business activity that directly competes with the Employer within a 50-mile radius.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(TERMINATION) Tj T*
(After the probationary period, either party may terminate this contract with thirty \(30\) days) Tj T*
(written notice. The Employer may terminate immediately for cause, including gross misconduct,) Tj T*
(fraud, or material breach of this Agreement.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(GOVERNING LAW) Tj T*
(This contract is governed by the laws of the State of California.) Tj T*
